diff --git a/tests/focaltech_moh-match/README.md b/tests/focaltech_moh-match/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..b5e17d82
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/focaltech_moh-match/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+Presses for `test-focaltech-moh-match`
+=====================================
+
+`presses.raw` holds 33 frames of 96x96 bytes, as the FT9201 behind the old
+SIU bridge (2808:93a9) delivers them, one after another:
+
+| frames | what |
+|---|---|
+| 0-14 | finger A, enrolment |
+| 15-20 | finger A, a later session |
+| 21-26 | finger B, of another person |
+| 27-32 | finger C, A's twin: the same ridge flow and spacing, other detail |
+
+They are **synthetic**: no one's fingerprint. They were drawn by an
+implementation of the method of SFinGe (Cappelli, Maio, Maltoni, "Synthetic
+fingerprint-database generation", ICPR 2002): an orientation field from the
+zero-pole model, a ridge pattern grown by iterated Gabor filtering, and each
+press a crop with natural placement, rotation, skin distortion, dry patches
+and sensor noise. The generator, and the script that wrote this file with a
+fixed seed (`synth/make_test_presses.py`), are in the ft9201-lab repository
+published with the merge request that added this test.
+
+Only probes the matcher decides with a margin were kept, so that the test
+does not depend on the last bit of a floating point result.
